Bugfix: Store an empty file cache mimetype as unknown

A storage backend reporting an empty mimetype ('' or null) reached the
mimetype loader, which registered an empty string as a new mimetype and stored
it as mimetype and mimepart of the file; null additionally raised deprecation
messages. Empty mimetypes are now stored as unknown (-1), like a mimetype of
false already was. This also covers updates on Oracle, where empty strings are
turned into null before they are stored.
